    "result_text": "The full suite (the single `AcceptanceTest`, backed by `AcceptanceBase`) passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a derived, read-only `telephoneDisplay` field to owner responses while leaving raw `telephone` in E.164 form.\n\n**What I changed:**\n\n1. **`util/Telephone.java` (new)** \u2014 a small utility owning E.164 country-code knowledge as the single source of truth. `display(\"+61412345678\")` \u2192 `\"+61 412 345 678\"`: splits the recognized country code, then groups the national digits left-to-right in threes. An unrecognized code isn't split out (all digits grouped); `null` in \u2192 `null` out.\n\n2. **`TelephoneNormalizer.java`** \u2014 removed its private duplicate of the country-code table and now delegates to `Telephone.countryCode` / `Telephone.nationalLength`, so normalization and display share one table instead of copying it.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `telephoneDisplay` mapping backed by a one-line `default` helper `Telephone.display(owner.getTelephone())`, matching how the other derived fields (`displayName`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, \u2026) are wired.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `telephoneDisplay` as a `readOnly` string on the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived response fields, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the getter/setter MapStruct populates.\n\nThe formatting logic lives in the `util` package where the mapper and the normalizer can both reach it, each class keeps a single responsibility, and the country-code table is defined in exactly one place. The `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` case (`0412 345 678` \u2192 `telephone=+61412345678`, `telephoneDisplay=+61 412 345 678`) passes, and the full build is green.",
